                <pb facs="0485" n="475" sameAs="frus:frus1919Parisv08/pg475"/>

                <head>Appendix E to HD–64</head>
                <p rendition="#flush"><hi rendition="#small-caps">u. s. naval communication service
                        paris, france</hi></p>
                <p rendition="#center"><hi rendition="#italic">Telegram</hi></p>
                <p rendition="#flush">From: Budapest.</p>
                <p rendition="#flush">To: Communication Section, Supreme Economic Council,
                    Paris.</p>
                <p>The opening of Danube has caused great activity in shipping circles. New Danubian
                    states and British shipping companies engaged in negotiations for transfer of
                    shipping from former owners are unable to complete transactions and commerce
                    operations owing to doubtful title of ships in river. It is imperative for
                    welfare of all Danubian countries and river navigation that the American
                    Arbitrator referred to in treaty should commence his arbitrage with the least
                    possible delay. No. 44.</p>
                <closer><hi rendition="#small-caps">Admiral</hi>
                    <signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Troubridge</hi></signed><anchor n="8"
                        xml:id="d23-f1"/></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d23-f1" n="8" xml:id="d23-f1-content">
                <p>Admiral Sir Ernest C. T. Troubridge, British Admiral commanding on the
                    Danube.</p>
            </note>
